 "notes": "Top-task-first (GOV.UK / Canada.ca / BC Gov): each of the ten most frequent tasks is 0-1 taps from any page, never more than 2. Utility bar on every page: Student Absent? (tap to call, Ext. 1), the three sign-ins (MyEducation BC, School Cash Online, Office 365) and Contact Us, beside the existing Translate and Search blocks; on phones a sticky bottom bar (Student Absent?, Translate, Search, Menu). Sign-ins stay apart from the help pages about them. Primary = 7 items by use; 'Home' goes (the crest links home) and the vague 'Information' bucket is split by task: Bell Schedule, PLT and Snow and Extreme Weather Protocols to School Calendar; Contact Us, Our Staff, Mission Statement, Catchment to About Us; Donations and District Concussion Protocol to Parents. Top labels link to their hub, a separate toggle opens the panel. groups[0] (no heading) = the section's top tasks, flagged 'featured' (Drupal menu_link_attributes class) and shown first, like Canada.ca 'Most requested'; other groups use existing headings only. Hubs render the same menu subtree (core menu block), so menu and hub never drift; the home page gets an 8+8 Parents/Students task band. All 20 orphans are in the menu; a few pages are cross-listed for a second audience. Labels = page titles ('Grad 2026' -> 'Grad 2027'), except the live menu words 'Bell Schedule', 'Library' and 'Catchment'. Clean aliases replace '-0', /node/, /media/, /library/q and /information/*; Redirect keeps old URLs. Retired with redirects: /information and /information-0, /media/1069, the duplicate '...-calendars-0' post, and two pages that are empty on the live site (Research & Inquiry, PAC Constitution and Bylaws) until they get content. No body or title changes."
}
